On Tuesday 11 January 2011 17:08:04 ianek wrote:
> I wonder if Lojban permits lujvo to be composed only from cmavo. Lujvo
> are brivla, so things like pavroi shouldn't work. But some cmavo
> contructs work as selbri, so rolmoi and nunrolmoi and such should
> work, no? I looked in CLL and I haven't found any statement about
> lujvo having to contain a gismu rafsi.

"pavroi" is a valid lujvo, as are "depybu'i" and "comdaidza" and "selke'e" 
and "pezmoi". What sort of place structure to assign to them is unclear. I 
use "comdaidza" and the like for "thingumbob".

